---
// /resume, "Me at Work": Alex's own words on each place he has worked,
// hand-written here (source: Me_at_work.md). The record itself is the PDF.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContentPage from '../components/ContentPage.astro';
import { APP_ROUTES } from '../config/site.js';

const external = { target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener noreferrer' };
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Me at Work — Alex Gao"
  description="Alex Gao (alexgaoth): his resume, and what he thought about working at Hypercubic, IBM and Signalor."
  keywords={['Alex Gao', 'alexgaoth', 'resume', 'Hypercubic', 'IBM', 'Signalor']}
  path={APP_ROUTES.resume}
>
  <ContentPage>
    <h1 class="title-page">Me at Work</h1>
    <p class="mb-small">
      here is my <a href="https://alexgaoth.com/resume.pdf" {...external}>resume</a>
    </p>
    <div class="space-y-large">
      <section>
        <h2 class="title-section">Experience</h2>
        <p class="mb-medium">
          rather than just relisting my resume in a in-style DOM, below is what i thought about each experience
        </p>

        <div class="experience-item">
          <div class="experience-header">
            <h3 class="experience-role">Hypercubic</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-small">
            <p class="text-gray">
              Working here match almost exactly to what i imagined. An early stage startup that moving at terminal velocity.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray">
              Burning tokens at a rate where most dont in a month or many, I was still surprised at the amount of work i get done per day. Other than scoping and architecting the actual work, most of the thinking is a continuous search of bottlenecks.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray">
              It is the increasing the change of acceleration, what i call on the job, increasing the <a class="dark" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerk_(physics)" {...external}>jerk</a>
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray">
              I liked our office. The mold allegation might be true or might not be, but I dont really feel it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="experience-item">
          <div class="experience-header">
            <h3 class="experience-role">IBM</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-small">
            <p class="text-gray">
              The campus of <a class="dark" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=555+Bailey+Avenue%2C+San+Jose%2C+CA" {...external}>555 Bailey Avenue</a>, and it's surrounding hills, lives in my mind as the definition of what dry California look like.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray">
              The campus doesn't have free catering (paid ones are unanimously tasteless), so I had to source my own food.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray">
              so apologies to the 10 group lunch and 5 potlucks I have invaded.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray">
              People here, especially my team, are very nice.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="experience-item">
          <div class="experience-header">
            <h3 class="experience-role">Signalor</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-small">
            <p class="text-gray">
              I have noticed that most (practically all) of my intellectually rigorous, high agency friend have the intuitive thought about a world where everyone is a founder (albeit many of them aren't one). Most of them would dismiss it with various reasons, but why they felt it to begin with, is revealing.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray">
              Founding a company, as it might be cliche to the pg essay readers, is one of the most rewarding thing a person can do in their life. Out of altruistic intentions, many would wish this on the rest of the population.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray">
              I dont hide this, Signalor was founded from the wrong heuristic, me and matthieu we just wanted to build, however that doesn't mean I don't believe in this venture. The people always come before the idea, and what we did the past year deems nothing but success for Signalor in the future.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </ContentPage>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Links in the reflections are dark, like the words around them; only the
     resume link keeps the browser's link colour. Hover inverts, as elsewhere. */
  .dark {
    color: #000;
    transition: background 0.12s, color 0.12s;
  }
  .dark:hover {
    background: #000;
    color: #fff;
  }
</style>
